# Next.js conventions

Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before changing App Router APIs — this Next version may differ from training data.

## Server vs client

- **Server** (default): pages, layouts, loaders (`getHomeContent()`, `getAllPosts()`, `getAllPeople()`, `getPage()`)
- **Client** (`"use client"`): `Header`, `HomeView`, `FadeIn`, `Tip`, `GalleryMosaic` (uses Next Image)
- Load markdown on server → pass props to client components
- `node:fs` only in `markdown.ts`, `content.ts`, `posts.ts`, `daily.ts`, `people.ts`, `pages.ts`, `essays.ts`

## Adding a page

1. `src/app/<route>/page.tsx` — call content loaders, render with `FadeIn` + `site-shell`
2. Export `metadata` from page or layout
3. Add URL in `src/app/sitemap.ts` (use `pageSlugs`, `getAllPosts()`, or `getAllPeople()`)
4. If markdown agents should not 404 it, update path checks in `src/proxy.ts`

## Blog / people

- Blog slugs: `content/blog/my-post.mdx` with `kind: note` → `/blog/my-post`
- Essay slugs: `content/blog/my-essay.mdx` with `kind: essay` → `/essays/my-essay` via `essays.ts`
- Gratitude slugs: `content/people/hackclub.mdx` → `/people/hackclub` via `people.ts`
- Trust pages: `content/pages/{about,contact,privacy}.mdx` → `pages.ts` → `src/app/[slug]/page.tsx` + `/{slug}.md`

## Preserve agent infrastructure

- `src/lib/discovery.ts` — llms.txt, profile, RSS
- `src/lib/agentic.ts` — Accept negotiation helpers
- `src/proxy.ts` — markdown rewrite for `/` and 404 markdown
- `src/app/sitemap.ts` — all indexable HTML URLs
- `scripts/test-agentic.mjs` — smoke tests; update when routes/sections change

## Config

- Images: Cloudinary host in `next.config.ts` remotePatterns
- Do not remove SEO routes: robots, sitemap, manifest, og/twitter images
